---
title: Prawn Fried Rice
servings: 1
course: dinner
tags: quick, 15 minutes
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/M-PuGg7Ek-w/maxresdefault.jpg
source: https://youtu.be/M-PuGg7Ek-w
time: 15m
---

For the dipping sauce, finely slice @bird's eye chilli{1} and mix in a #small bowl{} with @fish sauce{1%tbsp}, the juice of @lime{1}, and @sugar{0.5%tsp} until dissolved.

Thinly slice @shallot{1}. Mince @garlic{1%clove} and place it with thawed @raw prawn{100%g}. Roughly chop the leaves of @choy sum{2%stalks} and cut the stems into 1 cm pieces. Thinly slice @cucumber{0.5} into rounds for garnish.

Heat a #wok{} over high heat until smoking. Add @peanut oil{1%tbsp}, then add the shallots and choy sum stems. Stir-fry for ~{1%minute} with a pinch of @salt.

Add the garlic and prawns, stir-frying for ~{45%seconds} until the prawns turn pink, then push everything to one side of the wok.

Add the remaining @&peanut oil{1%tbsp} to the clear side. Crack in @egg{1}, break the yolk, and let set briefly before scrambling and tossing together with the prawns.

Add cold @cooked rice{1%bowl}, @oyster sauce{1%tbsp}, @white pepper{0.25%tsp}, and the chopped choy sum leaves. Toss constantly over high heat for ~{2%minutes} until thoroughly heated through.

Transfer the fried rice to a #plate{} and serve with sliced cucumber and the prepared dipping sauce.
